window.portfolioEnglish={"sections": {"home": "<p class=\"eyebrow\">MOHAMED YASSINE AYACHE · CAREER GOAL: IT SYSTEM INTEGRATION</p><h1 id=\"home-title\">Linux. Networks.<br><em>System integration.</em></h1><p class=\"intro\">My goal is to start a career in IT system integration in Germany. My project experience includes hardening Debian servers, building containerized services, and configuring IPv4 networks.</p><p class=\"profile-badge\">German B2 · English C1 · Learning through projects</p><button class=\"primary\" data-go=\"work\">Explore my projects <span>↗</span></button><div class=\"start-links\" aria-label=\"CV and GitHub\"><a href=\"https://ik.imagekit.io/szcfr7vth/Yassine_Ayache_CV.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CV · English ↗</a><a href=\"https://ik.imagekit.io/szcfr7vth/Yassine_Ayache_lebenslauf.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lebenslauf · Deutsch ↗</a><a href=\"https://github.com/mayachee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub ↗</a></div>", "work": "<p class=\"eyebrow\">01 / PRACTICAL SYSTEM INTEGRATION</p><h2 id=\"work-title\">Build servers.<br><em>Understand connections.</em></h2><p class=\"intro\">My own server, container, and networking projects are the focus. Each case study explains the task, implementation, and relevance to IT operations.</p><div class=\"project-actions\"><button data-project=\"born2beroot\"><span>01</span><strong>Born2beroot</strong><small>12/2022 · Debian · SSH / UFW · Monitoring</small><b>↗</b></button><button data-project=\"inception\"><span>02</span><strong>Inception</strong><small>03/2025 · Docker Compose · Nginx / TLS</small><b>↗</b></button><button data-project=\"netpractice\"><span>03</span><strong>NetPractice</strong><small>10/2023 · IPv4 · CIDR · Routing · 10 levels</small><b>↗</b></button><button data-project=\"transcendence\"><span>04</span><strong>ft_transcendence</strong><small>04/2025 · Team project · Authentication</small><b>↗</b></button><button data-project=\"irc\"><span>05</span><strong>ft_irc</strong><small>02/2025 · C++98 · TCP sockets</small><b>↗</b></button></div><p class=\"small-note\">More integration experience: <button class=\"inline-case\" data-project=\"studio\">Scripts Studio ↗</button> and <button class=\"inline-case\" data-project=\"airbcar\">AIRBCAR ↗</button>. The case studies explain my technical approach and the components involved.</p>", "systems": "<p class=\"eyebrow\">02 / SKILLS & DEVELOPMENT</p><h2 id=\"systems-title\">Solid foundations.<br><em>Keep building.</em></h2><ul class=\"skill-list\"><li><span>LINUX & SERVER HARDENING / BORN2BEROOT</span>Debian / VirtualBox · SSH · UFW · Password & sudo policies · cron monitoring</li><li><span>CONTAINERS & SERVICES / INCEPTION</span>Docker Compose · Nginx / TLS · WordPress / MariaDB · Volumes / networks / secrets</li><li><span>NETWORKING & TROUBLESHOOTING / NETPRACTICE</span>IPv4 · Subnetting / CIDR · Routing tables · 10 completed levels</li><li><span>NEXT LEARNING GOALS</span>Windows Server / Active Directory · Microsoft 365 / Entra ID · Backup & restore tests · Support documentation</li></ul><button class=\"outline\" data-project=\"lab\">Next step: an extended infrastructure lab ↗</button><p class=\"small-note\">The Linux, container, and networking projects are complete. The additional Windows/operations lab is planned; these new topics are learning goals.</p>", "about": "<p class=\"eyebrow\">03 / MY PATH TO SYSTEM INTEGRATION</p><h2 id=\"about-title\">Understand technology.<br><em>Connect systems.</em></h2><p class=\"intro\">I’m Mohamed Yassine Ayache — MAYACHE. My focus for starting a career in Germany is IT system integration, with Linux, container, and networking experience from my own projects.</p><p class=\"body-copy\">I built my technical background at 1337 Coding School and OFPPT. Born2beroot, Inception, and NetPractice connect server configuration, hardening, and network analysis. The team project ft_transcendence brought together authentication, WebSockets, and Docker.</p><p class=\"body-copy\">I also bring development experience from AIRBCAR, ft_irc, and Scripts Studio. My next step is to extend these foundations with Windows/identity management, verified recovery, and clear operational documentation.</p><p class=\"languages\">German B2 · English C1 · Arabic native · French basic</p><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"https://ik.imagekit.io/szcfr7vth/Yassine_Ayache_CV.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Read my English CV ↗</a>", "contact": "<p class=\"eyebrow\">04 / STARTING A CAREER IN GERMANY</p><h2 id=\"contact-title\">Learn together.<br><em>Build better IT.</em></h2><p class=\"intro\">Looking for a motivated entry-level candidate in IT system integration? I’d be happy to discuss my project experience and next learning goals.</p><a class=\"primary\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mayachee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a><div class=\"socials\"><a href=\"https://github.com/mayachee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub ↗</a><a href=\"https://ik.imagekit.io/szcfr7vth/Yassine_Ayache_lebenslauf.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CV DE ↗</a><a href=\"https://ik.imagekit.io/szcfr7vth/Yassine_Ayache_CV.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CV EN ↗</a></div>"}, "cases": {"born2beroot": {"eyebrow": "SERVER ADMINISTRATION PROJECT / 12/2022", "title": "Born2beroot — a hardened Linux server", "intro": "Planned, installed, configured, and secured a Debian server in VirtualBox.", "body": "<div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>Server setup</h3><p>Set up Debian as a virtual machine in VirtualBox and implemented the system configuration and administrative requirements in my own project.</p><h3>Hardening</h3><p>Configured SSH on a custom port, UFW firewall rules, and strict password and sudo policies. The custom SSH port complements the access configuration; it does not replace access controls.</p></section><section><h3>Monitoring & services</h3><p>Used a monitoring script scheduled with cron for regular system checks. The bonus included WordPress with Lighttpd, MariaDB, and PHP.</p><h3>Relevance to system integration</h3><p>Practical foundations in Linux administration, virtualization, secure configuration, and recurring system checks.</p></section></div><div class=\"tags\"><span>Debian</span><span>VirtualBox</span><span>SSH</span><span>UFW</span><span>sudo</span><span>cron</span><span>Lighttpd / MariaDB / PHP</span></div>"}, "inception": {"eyebrow": "CONTAINERIZED INFRASTRUCTURE / 03/2025", "title": "Inception — services as a connected system", "intro": "Built a complete web stack with Docker Compose: Nginx, WordPress, and MariaDB in separate containers.", "body": "<div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>Architecture</h3><p>Connected the services with Docker Compose. Used Alpine Linux as part of the container environment and separated the web server, application, and database responsibilities.</p><h3>Configuration</h3><p>Configured SSL/TLS at Nginx, persistent data volumes, Docker networks, and credentials using secrets.</p></section><section><h3>Understanding dependencies</h3><p>The project connects service configuration, communication between containers, encrypted access, and persistent storage.</p><h3>Relevance to system integration</h3><p>Experience with interdependent services and reproducible deployment.</p></section></div><div class=\"tags\"><span>Docker Compose</span><span>Nginx</span><span>TLS</span><span>WordPress</span><span>MariaDB</span><span>Alpine Linux</span><span>Volumes / networks / secrets</span></div>"}, "netpractice": {"eyebrow": "NETWORKING FUNDAMENTALS / 10/2023", "title": "NetPractice — understand IPv4 and find faults", "intro": "Completed ten networking levels covering IPv4, subnetting, and routing.", "body": "<div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>Configuration</h3><p>Configured networks using CIDR subnet masks, switches, routers, and routing tables.</p><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>Analyzed misconfigurations and restored connectivity within the networking exercises. Completed all ten levels.</p></section><section><h3>Relevance to system integration</h3><p>Addressing, subnet boundaries, and routes provide a foundation for structured analysis of connectivity problems.</p><h3>Project context</h3><p>A configuration and practice project with ten completed levels, focused on understandable addressing and reachability.</p></section></div><div class=\"tags\"><span>IPv4</span><span>Subnetting / CIDR</span><span>Routing</span><span>Troubleshooting</span><span>10 levels</span></div>"}, "transcendence": {"eyebrow": "TEAM PROJECT / 04/2025", "title": "ft_transcendence — a secure real-time platform", "intro": "Worked in a team on a real-time platform with Django, WebSockets, PostgreSQL, and Docker.", "body": "<div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>Authentication</h3><p>The team project includes secure login with OAuth 2.0, JWT, and two-factor authentication.</p><h3>Real time & deployment</h3><p>Real-time games over WebSockets and the application running in Docker containers.</p></section><section><h3>Relevance to system integration</h3><p>The interaction of application, database, communication, and login, alongside teamwork on a system with several components.</p><h3>My context</h3><p>This is a team project. The features describe the shared result, rather than claiming that I implemented every component alone.</p></section></div><div class=\"tags\"><span>Django</span><span>WebSockets</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>Docker</span><span>OAuth 2.0 / JWT / 2FA</span><span>Teamwork</span></div>"}, "irc": {"eyebrow": "SERVER & PROTOCOL DEVELOPMENT / 02/2025", "title": "ft_irc — my own IRC server", "intro": "Developed an IRC server in C++98 using TCP sockets, compatible with a standard IRC client.", "body": "<div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>Implementation</h3><p>Server development using TCP sockets and the IRC protocol. Compatibility with a standard IRC client was part of the project.</p></section><section><h3>Relevance to system integration</h3><p>Practical understanding of client-server communication and network services. Developing a server complements my administration experience from Born2beroot.</p></section></div><div class=\"tags\"><span>C++98</span><span>TCP sockets</span><span>IRC</span><span>Client-server</span></div>"}, "studio": {"eyebrow": "PROJECT EXPERIENCE / AUTOMATION & INTEGRATION", "title": "Scripts Studio", "intro": "A local workspace connecting separate media tools through a shared interface and Python runner.", "body": "<img src=\"/assets/studio-preview.png\" alt=\"Actual Scripts Studio interface\"><div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>The problem</h3><p>Individual scripts had different entry points and inputs. Results had to be passed manually between tools.</p><h3>My contribution</h3><p>Organized tools into a shared interface for video creation, clip discovery and downloading, media checks, and output cleanup. Python, PowerShell, and FFmpeg are part of the project environment.</p></section><section><h3>Relevance to system integration</h3><p>Integrating external tools, automating repeatable steps, and making failures traceable through logs and job history. Media validation, process cancellation, and cleanup previews support controlled workflows.</p><h3>Project context</h3><p>A local software and integration project focused on process control and traceable workflows.</p></section></div><div class=\"tags\"><span>Python</span><span>PowerShell</span><span>Process control</span><span>Logs & troubleshooting</span><span>Tool integration</span></div>"}, "airbcar": {"eyebrow": "PROJECT EXPERIENCE / APPLICATION INTEGRATION / 2025", "title": "AIRBCAR", "intro": "A rental platform connecting customers and rental agencies in Morocco.", "body": "<div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>Task & contribution</h3><p>UI/UX design and frontend development, alongside backend integration with Django and PostgreSQL. The work included booking workflows and role-based access inside the application.</p><h3>Technical components</h3><p>Django APIs and PostgreSQL, complemented by Supabase and Redis. Docker and GitHub Actions were part of the deployment workflows.</p></section><section><h3>Relevance to system integration</h3><p>Understanding interfaces and dependencies between the application, data, and deployment. This provides a starting point for learning operations, monitoring, and structured fault diagnosis.</p><h3>Project context</h3><p>The project connects interfaces, APIs, storage, and deployment. My additional infrastructure projects demonstrate server and networking experience.</p></section></div><div class=\"tags\"><span>API integration</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>Docker</span><span>GitHub Actions</span><span>Application roles</span></div>"}, "lab": {"eyebrow": "PLANNED / IT SYSTEM INTEGRATION LEARNING PATH", "title": "Infrastructure lab: from plan to evidence", "intro": "A planned extension of my existing Linux, container, and networking experience. This additional lab has not yet been implemented; the following items are learning goals and planned evidence.", "body": "<p class=\"case-note\">Status: planned. Building on my existing projects, I want to practice identity management and operational workflows in a shared test environment.</p><figure class=\"lab-map\"><figcaption>Planned lab — target architecture, not built yet</figcaption><svg viewBox=\"0 0 660 190\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Planned test environment: Windows client, internal network, Windows and Linux servers, monitoring and backup\"><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6aafa3\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M150 90H255M325 60V32H480V60M325 120V157H480V120\"/></g><g fill=\"#142e3e\" stroke=\"#5a8b8c\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"140\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"255\" y=\"60\" width=\"140\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"6\" width=\"240\" height=\"55\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"126\" width=\"240\" height=\"55\" rx=\"6\"/></g><g fill=\"#dcf5ed\" font-family=\"Segoe UI, sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"85\">Windows client</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"105\">Test user</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"85\">Internal test network</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"105\">DNS / DHCP</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"30\">Windows / Linux</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"49\">Identities / services</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"150\">Monitoring / Backup</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"169\">Alert / restore test</text></g></svg></figure><div class=\"case-grid\"><section><h3>01 / Networks & virtualization</h3><p>Build an isolated virtual environment with an IP plan, subnets, DNS, and DHCP. Evidence: a network diagram and documented diagnosis of a DNS fault.</p><h3>02 / Windows & identities</h3><p>Connect Windows Server and a client using Active Directory, test accounts, groups, shares, and group policies. Evidence: an access matrix, onboarding/offboarding checklist, and access tests.</p><h3>03 / Linux & automation</h3><p>Operate a Linux service, check permissions and updates, and create inventory and health reports with PowerShell/Python. Evidence: configuration, a script, and a traceable test run.</p></section><section><h3>04 / Monitoring & IT support</h3><p>Observe availability and investigate a controlled service failure. Evidence: a ticket covering symptoms, diagnosis, root cause, resolution, and a clear update to the user.</p><h3>05 / Security & recovery</h3><p>Limit access, document patch status, and test backup and restoration. Evidence: a restore report with validation results; a snapshot alone is not a backup test.</p><h3>06 / Microsoft 365 & handover</h3><p>Learn user, licensing, and identity fundamentals in Microsoft 365/Entra ID if a suitable test environment is available. Evidence: a documented exercise and short operations guide.</p></section></div><p class=\"case-note\">Build on Born2beroot, Inception, and NetPractice: document a shared test environment, then add Windows/AD and a verified restore. Only tested results will be published as completed project experience.</p>"}}};
